Subject: wasix: support multiple epoll registrations per file

The virtual epoll kept one interest registration per file, so adding
the same file to a second epoll instance displaced the first waiter,
and one readiness transition woke only one set. Linux gives each epoll
instance its own registration, and multi-process servers rely on that:
a latch self-pipe sits in several wait-event sets, and a signal
handler's write must wake whichever set is being waited on. Keep an
EpollInterestRegistry of independent registrations per file and fan
readiness out to every interested epoll instance. Every subscription
reinstalls a socket source's selector registration, so one that
arrives on a live descriptor - an interest switch after a request -
snapshots the level-triggered readiness it joined.

